==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|lecherous|lang=enm}}, {{term|licherous|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{recons|lecherous|lang=fro}} (attested in {{etyl|fro|-}} {{term|lecherousement||lecherously|lang=fro}}), from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|lecherie|lang=fro}}, {{term|licherie||gluttony, sensuality, lewdness, lechery|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|lecher|lang=fro}}, {{term|lechier|lang=fro}}, {{term|lekier|lang=fro}}, {{term|lescher||to lick, live in gluttony or sensuality|lang=fro}}, from Old {{etyl|frk}} {{recons|lekkon|lekkōn|to lick|lang=frk}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro}} {{recons|likkōnan||to lick|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro}} {{recons|leyǵʰ-||to lick|lang=ine-pro}}, equivalent to {{suffix|lecher|ous}}. More at {{l|en|lick}}.

